{
 "format": "mainaiger",
 "schema_version": 2,
 "notebook": {
  "nbformat": 4,
  "nbformat_minor": 5,
  "metadata": {
   "kernelspec": {
    "name": "python3",
    "display_name": "Python 3",
    "language": "python"
   },
   "mainaiger": {
    "example": true,
    "name": "self-improve",
    "title": "Self-improvement loop (propose, try on a copy, judge, loop)"
   }
  },
  "cells": [
   {
    "id": "readme",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "How this loop works"
     }
    },
    "source": "# The first self-improvement loop\n\n**Propose** (a model rewrites the training cell) → **Apply to copy** (the proposal runs on a copy of the session, never touching the baseline) → **Judge** (a model reads the numbers and says keep / revert / ask) → **Report**. The dashed arrow from Judge back to Propose is a *loop arrow*: while the verdict is not \"keep\" it sends the run back for another proposal, at most twice (its budget), and the previous attempt is pasted into the next prompt so the model does not repeat itself. Then Report prints every attempt.\n\nYou approve the run; keeping a change is your decision: paste the proposed code into the training cell, or push it to the Library as a new version. Every step is on this canvas and in the Log.\n\nThe baseline is deliberately undertrained (10 epochs, a tiny learning rate), so there is something to improve. Needs: a running session and an installed Ollama model named in the two model cells (Models page). Without a model the two model cells stop the run with a plain error.\n",
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "load",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Load data",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [
       "rows"
      ]
     }
    },
    "source": "import random\nrandom.seed(7)\n# Synthetic dataset: two blobs in 2-D. Replace with a real loader; keep `rows` as [(features, label), ...].\nrows = []\nfor _ in range(200):\n    label = random.randint(0, 1)\n    centre = (0.0, 0.0) if label == 0 else (2.0, 1.5)\n    rows.append(([random.gauss(centre[0], 1.0), random.gauss(centre[1], 1.0)], label))\nprint(f\"loaded {len(rows)} rows, {sum(r[1] for r in rows)} positive\")\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "features",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Extract features",
      "inputs": [
       "rows"
      ],
      "outputs": [
       "X",
       "y",
       "feature_names"
      ]
     }
    },
    "source": "# From rows -> X (list of feature lists) and y (labels). Adds x1*x2 and standardises columns.\nraw = [feat + [feat[0] * feat[1]] for feat, _ in rows]\ny = [label for _, label in rows]\ncols = list(zip(*raw))\nmeans = [sum(c) / len(c) for c in cols]\nstds = [max(1e-9, (sum((v - m) ** 2 for v in c) / len(c)) ** 0.5) for c, m in zip(cols, means)]\nX = [[(v - m) / s for v, m, s in zip(r, means, stds)] for r in raw]\nfeature_names = [\"x1\", \"x2\", \"x1*x2\"]\nprint(f\"{len(X)} samples x {len(feature_names)} features: {feature_names}\")\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "split",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Split train/test",
      "inputs": [
       "X",
       "y"
      ],
      "outputs": [
       "X_train",
       "y_train",
       "X_test",
       "y_test"
      ]
     }
    },
    "source": "import random\nrng = random.Random(42)\norder = list(range(len(X)))\nrng.shuffle(order)\ncut = int(len(order) * 0.75)\nX_train = [X[i] for i in order[:cut]]; y_train = [y[i] for i in order[:cut]]\nX_test = [X[i] for i in order[cut:]]; y_test = [y[i] for i in order[cut:]]\nprint(f\"train {len(X_train)} / test {len(X_test)}\")\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "train",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Train classifier (baseline)",
      "inputs": [
       "X_train",
       "y_train"
      ],
      "outputs": [
       "model"
      ]
     }
    },
    "source": "import math\n# Logistic regression, gradient descent, standard library only.\n# Deliberately undertrained (few epochs, small learning rate): the loop's job is to improve it.\nweights = [0.0] * len(X_train[0]); bias = 0.0; lr = 0.01\nfor epoch in range(10):\n    grad_w = [0.0] * len(weights); grad_b = 0.0\n    for xi, yi in zip(X_train, y_train):\n        z = sum(w * v for w, v in zip(weights, xi)) + bias\n        p = 1 / (1 + math.exp(-z))\n        err = p - yi\n        for j, v in enumerate(xi):\n            grad_w[j] += err * v\n        grad_b += err\n    n = len(X_train)\n    weights = [w - lr * g / n for w, g in zip(weights, grad_w)]\n    bias -= lr * grad_b / n\ndef predict(x):\n    return 1 if sum(w * v for w, v in zip(weights, x)) + bias > 0 else 0\nmodel = {\"weights\": weights, \"bias\": bias, \"predict\": predict}\nprint(\"weights\", [round(w, 3) for w in weights], \"bias\", round(bias, 3))\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "evaluate",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Evaluate",
      "inputs": [
       "model",
       "X_test",
       "y_test"
      ],
      "outputs": [
       "metrics"
      ]
     }
    },
    "source": "pred = [model[\"predict\"](x) for x in X_test]\ntp = sum(1 for p, t in zip(pred, y_test) if p == 1 and t == 1)\ntn = sum(1 for p, t in zip(pred, y_test) if p == 0 and t == 0)\nfp = sum(1 for p, t in zip(pred, y_test) if p == 1 and t == 0)\nfn = sum(1 for p, t in zip(pred, y_test) if p == 0 and t == 1)\nprecision = tp / (tp + fp) if tp + fp else 0.0\nrecall = tp / (tp + fn) if tp + fn else 0.0\nmetrics = {\"accuracy\": (tp + tn) / len(y_test), \"precision\": precision, \"recall\": recall,\n           \"f1\": 2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall) if precision + recall else 0.0,\n           \"confusion\": {\"tp\": tp, \"tn\": tn, \"fp\": fp, \"fn\": fn}}\nprint({k: (round(v, 3) if isinstance(v, float) else v) for k, v in metrics.items()})\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "propose",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Propose change",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [
       "proposal"
      ],
      "model": {
       "model": "qwen2.5-coder:7b",
       "output": "proposal",
       "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
         "source": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 40,
          "description": "the complete new training cell: every line of Python, not a language name or a fragment"
         },
         "why": {
          "type": "string",
          "maxLength": 300
         }
        },
        "required": [
         "source",
         "why"
        ]
       },
       "attempts": 2
      }
     }
    },
    "source": "You improve a small machine-learning training cell written in plain Python (standard library only, no numpy).\nHere are the baseline metrics the current cell achieved:\n{{output:Evaluate}}\n\nWhat the previous attempt did, if there was one (do not propose the same change again):\n{{output:Apply to copy}}\n\nReturn the whole rewritten cell in \"source\": every line of Python, ready to run; a language name or a fragment is not a cell. Here is the current training cell. It must keep defining `model` as a dict with \"weights\", \"bias\" and a \"predict\" function taking one feature list and returning 0 or 1. It may use the variables X_train and y_train only.\n----\nimport math\nweights = [0.0] * len(X_train[0]); bias = 0.0; lr = 0.01\nfor epoch in range(10):\n    grad_w = [0.0] * len(weights); grad_b = 0.0\n    for xi, yi in zip(X_train, y_train):\n        z = sum(w * v for w, v in zip(weights, xi)) + bias\n        p = 1 / (1 + math.exp(-z))\n        err = p - yi\n        for j, v in enumerate(xi):\n            grad_w[j] += err * v\n        grad_b += err\n    n = len(X_train)\n    weights = [w - lr * g / n for w, g in zip(weights, grad_w)]\n    bias -= lr * grad_b / n\ndef predict(x):\n    return 1 if sum(w * v for w, v in zip(weights, x)) + bias > 0 else 0\nmodel = {\"weights\": weights, \"bias\": bias, \"predict\": predict}\nprint(\"weights\", [round(w, 3) for w in weights], \"bias\", round(bias, 3))\n----\nPropose ONE small change that might improve accuracy (for example the learning rate, the number of epochs, or feature scaling inside the loop). Return the complete new cell source and one sentence why.",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "apply",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Apply to copy",
      "inputs": [
       "proposal",
       "X_test",
       "y_test",
       "metrics"
      ],
      "outputs": [
       "candidate_metrics"
      ]
     }
    },
    "source": "# Run the proposal on a COPY of this session's variables; the baseline `model` is untouched.\n# `history` remembers every attempt of this run, so Report can list them.\ntry:\n    history\nexcept NameError:\n    history = []\nMIN_GAIN = 0.02  # the same bar the Judge prompt states\ncandidate_ns = {k: v for k, v in globals().items() if not k.startswith(\"_\")}\ntry:\n    exec(proposal[\"source\"], candidate_ns)\n    candidate = candidate_ns[\"model\"]\n    pred = [candidate[\"predict\"](x) for x in X_test]\n    tp = sum(1 for p, t in zip(pred, y_test) if p == 1 and t == 1); tn = sum(1 for p, t in zip(pred, y_test) if p == 0 and t == 0)\n    candidate_metrics = {\"accuracy\": (tp + tn) / len(y_test)}\n    print(\"attempt %d\" % (len(history) + 1))\n    print(\"why:\", proposal[\"why\"])\n    print(\"baseline accuracy: %.3f\" % metrics[\"accuracy\"])\n    print(\"candidate accuracy: %.3f\" % candidate_metrics[\"accuracy\"])\n    print(\"delta: %+.3f\" % (candidate_metrics[\"accuracy\"] - metrics[\"accuracy\"]))\n    # The harness's own gate, computed from the numbers: the judge's verdict is never the only check.\n    improved = candidate_metrics[\"accuracy\"] >= metrics[\"accuracy\"] + MIN_GAIN\nexcept Exception as error:\n    candidate_metrics = {\"accuracy\": None, \"error\": \"%s: %s\" % (type(error).__name__, error)}\n    improved = False\n    print(\"attempt %d\" % (len(history) + 1))\n    print(\"the proposal failed:\", candidate_metrics[\"error\"])\nprint(\"improved by at least %+.2f: %s\" % (MIN_GAIN, improved))\nhistory.append({\"why\": proposal[\"why\"], \"accuracy\": candidate_metrics.get(\"accuracy\"), \"error\": candidate_metrics.get(\"error\"), \"improved\": improved, \"source\": proposal[\"source\"]})\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "judge",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Judge",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [
       "verdict"
      ],
      "model": {
       "model": "qwen2.5-coder:7b",
       "output": "verdict",
       "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
         "action": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
           "keep",
           "revert",
           "ask"
          ]
         },
         "confidence": {
          "type": "number"
         },
         "reasons": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
           "type": "string"
          },
          "maxItems": 3
         }
        },
        "required": [
         "action",
         "confidence"
        ]
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "source": "A proposed change to a training cell was tried on a copy. Here is what happened:\n{{output:Apply to copy}}\n\nDecide: \"keep\" only if the candidate accuracy is clearly better than the baseline (at least +0.02) and nothing failed; \"revert\" if it is worse or failed; \"ask\" if the difference is too small to tell.",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "report",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Report",
      "inputs": [
       "verdict",
       "metrics",
       "candidate_metrics",
       "proposal"
      ],
      "outputs": []
     }
    },
    "source": "print(\"=\" * 48)\nprint(\"Self-improvement loop: %d attempt%s\" % (len(history), \"\" if len(history) == 1 else \"s\"))\nprint(\"=\" * 48)\nprint(\"baseline accuracy: %.3f\" % metrics[\"accuracy\"])\nfor i, h in enumerate(history, 1):\n    shown = (\"accuracy %.3f (%+.3f)\" % (h[\"accuracy\"], h[\"accuracy\"] - metrics[\"accuracy\"])) if h[\"accuracy\"] is not None else \"failed: \" + str(h[\"error\"])\n    print(\"  %d. %s - %s\" % (i, shown, h[\"why\"]))\nprint(\"last verdict:\", verdict[\"action\"], \"(confidence %.2f)\" % verdict[\"confidence\"])\nfor r in verdict.get(\"reasons\", []):\n    print(\" -\", r)\nif verdict[\"action\"] == \"keep\" and not history[-1][\"improved\"]:\n    print()\n    print(\"The judge said keep, but the numbers do not show the +0.02 gain the rule asks for.\")\n    print(\"The harness does not accept a verdict the measurements contradict: the baseline stays.\")\n    print(\"(A small model often agrees too easily; the loop arrow sends the run back while this happens.)\")\nelif verdict[\"action\"] == \"keep\":\n    print()\n    print(\"To keep this change: paste the source below into 'Train classifier (baseline)',\")\n    print(\"or push it to the Library as a new version of train-classifier.\")\n    print(\"-\" * 48)\n    print(history[-1][\"source\"])\nelif verdict[\"action\"] == \"ask\":\n    print(\"Too close to call after the loop's budget: run again, or change the proposal prompt.\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Reverted every attempt: the baseline stays. Run again for new proposals.\")\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   }
  ]
 },
